# Prologue profile: safe minimal set for dump/restore (dump phase 1).
#
# Line 1 lists which .env/local/ OVERRIDES of the SOURCE are transferred at
# the very TOP of a dump, before any replayed command executes. The restore
# runs against the state bootstrap created (structure + init profile in
# .env/default/), so only source overrides need transferring -- and only
# those the restore itself depends on:
#
#   - base interpreters (global execution control; a source may have pinned
#     them, and the replay must run under the SAME model)
#   - build/deploy configuration (STAND_*_SUBDIRS, PKCS11_*, prerequisites)
#     that the emitted rebuild commands consume
#
# DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED: every function-specific ELEBAKE_INTERPRETER_<fn>
# override. Restoring one early could DEACTIVATE a replayed command (e.g. a
# cat pin on pem add would turn the key registration into a display) -- they
# are restored at the very END by the EPILOGUE, when the replay is done.
